## Warnings and Alerts

### Severity Levels

| Level | Use For |
|-------|---------|
| **Note** | General information, tips (low severity) |
| **Warning** | Potential issues if ignored (moderate severity) |
| **Danger** | Severe consequences possible (high severity) |

### Guidelines

- Always explain consequences
- Provide remediation steps when possible
- Keep warnings concise and actionable

**Example:**
> **Warning:** Disabling encryption may expose sensitive data. See [Security Guide](link) for alternatives.

---

## SEO Considerations

### Sentence Structure

Place keywords at the beginning of sentences:

- **Better:** "To create a new role, open Settings and click Add."
- **Worse:** "Open Settings and click Add to create a new role."

### Headers

- Include relevant keywords naturally
- Use structured hierarchy (H1 -> H2 -> H3)
- Avoid keyword stuffing

---

## Version Badges

When documenting features introduced in specific versions:

```markdown
## New Feature Name

*Available since v{version}*

Description of the feature...
```
